      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 1294: New concern (distinct from the already-noted items): deferring `isMessageTreated` past the async `findCertificate` removes the *synchronous* replay/duplicate suppression that previously ran for every call request. Two consequences: (1) DHT `listen` callbacks routinely fire multiple times for the same value, and multiple duplicate call requests that arrive within the cert-check window will now all reach `iOSConnectedCb_` — if that callback raises a CallKit signal, the extension can report the same incoming call several times. (2) On the untrusted path (`foundPeerDevice` fails), `isMessageTreated` is never reached, so a peer can replay the same `req.id` indefinitely, each replay spawning a fresh async certificate lookup with no dedup ceiling. Consider still recording/deduping the id synchronously (or immediately inside the cert callback before invoking `iOSConnectedCb_`) so that only the *marking-as-treated-for-the-main-app* is deferred, not the replay guard.",
      "revId": "f38bda683b6b84007cadf20387122ef95895baf0",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
    },
